<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who the Classic Series is for</h2>
        <p>The Classic Series is Nordic's signature round tub, the series that started the brand. It's for people who like sitting face to face, want easy entry, and prefer simple, powerful whirlpool therapy over lots of gadgets. Multi-level, barrier-free seating means everyone can find a comfortable depth, and double Nordic Star whirlpool jets on top models deliver a full-body soak.</p>
        <h2>Round tubs and small spaces</h2>
        <p>A round tub tucks neatly into a corner of a patio or deck. The Crown Classic is 84 inches across and 35 inches deep. The Impulse Classic is Nordic's shallowest model at 31 inches, which is easier to step into and a good choice for kids or anyone with limited mobility. Add sturdy <a href="/steps/">steps</a> for safe entry on icy evenings.</p>
        <h2>Electrical: most are convertible</h2>
        <p>Nordic lists most Classic Series models as <strong>110V/220V convertible</strong>, including the Impulse DP and Impulse Classic, with about a 1 kW heater on 110V and a 4 kW heater on 220V. You can start on a standard outlet and upgrade to 240V later for faster winter heat recovery. See <a href="/guides/110v-vs-240v-hot-tubs/">110V vs 240V</a>.</p>
        <h2>See the Classic Series in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit. For winter use, read our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">Utah winter guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

